# Line endings.
#
# Tests byte-compare generated files with the committed ones (`.actor/*`, `engines.json`, the pricing reference bodies), `sha256sum -c` checks the freeze manifest,
# and `apify push` uploads the working tree as it is. A checkout that turns LF into CRLF (Git for Windows defaults to core.autocrlf=true) therefore fails tests and uploads
# bytes that differ from the committed ones. Every platform must see LF in text files, whatever core.autocrlf says.
* text=auto eol=lf
*.ts text eol=lf
*.mjs text eol=lf
*.js text eol=lf
*.py text eol=lf
*.json text eol=lf
*.md text eol=lf
*.yml text eol=lf
*.yaml text eol=lf
*.toml text eol=lf
*.sh text eol=lf
*.sha256 text eol=lf
*.patch text eol=lf
Dockerfile text eol=lf
.dockerignore text eol=lf
.gitignore text eol=lf
.gitattributes text eol=lf

# Captured real responses and expected outputs are compared byte for byte: never normalised, on any platform.
master_engines/test/fixtures/** -text
master_engines/distribution/python/tests/fixtures/** -text
